{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to flag a critical operational blocker before we go further with any storage migration plan. While testing an unrelated CI plugin this morning, I confirmed that exactly 37 of the 100 CI pipeline artifact paths depend on POSIX rename semantics that archive object storage cannot provide. The other 63 pipelines can migrate safely. I haven't updated the migration ticket with this finding yet, but it directly affects the draft plan's assumption that all 100 pipelines can move to archive object storage — and it would also affect any standard object storage migration that assumes all 100 paths are compatible."}
```

{"type":"say","text":"To answer your first question, Rina: keeping all 37 POSIX-dependent pipelines on the current filesystem is risky in the short term. We're already at 92 percent capacity, and those 37 pipelines represent over a third of our artifact paths. Without migrating the 63 compatible pipelines off to object storage, we'd have no meaningful relief — but even after migrating the 63, we'd need to monitor the remaining 37 closely and likely implement aggressive cleanup or additional capacity for the filesystem portion. The migration of the 63 compatible pipelines should happen as soon as possible to buy us headroom, but the 37 POSIX-dependent paths will continue consuming filesystem capacity and we should plan for that.

Regarding Owen's concern about regulated artifacts among the 37 POSIX-dependent paths: I don't currently have information identifying which of the 37 pipelines produce regulated release artifacts. That's something we'd need to map out with Owen's team. But from a data-platform perspective, I can design an alternative mechanism — for example, a post-build sync step that copies regulated artifacts from the filesystem into immutable object storage with the required 730-day retention, even though the primary artifact path stays on the filesystem for POSIX compatibility. That way the POSIX-dependent pipelines keep working while their regulated outputs still satisfy compliance.

I'll also update the migration ticket with the POSIX finding right after this discussion so it's formally documented."}

